","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:5Flows3CutV","text":"Cut"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"C"},{"kind":"text","text":">?"}],"type":"topic","title":"minimumCut(capacity:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A minimum cut over all nonempty proper vertex sets S, by the capacity of the edges leaving"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"S (igraph "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"mincut()"},{"type":"text","text":" on a directed graph): Hao and Orlin’s algorithm (LEMON "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HaoOrlin"},{"type":"text","text":"),"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one push–relabel run that moves the sink through every vertex, then the same on the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reversed graph, so both the cuts with the first vertex on the source side and those with it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"on the sink side are seen. Which minimum cut is returned when several exist is not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"specified, but the same input always gives the same cut. nil below two vertices."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"capacity"},{"type":"text","text":" is called once per non-loop edge, in position order, before any work."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"O(n²m) in the worst case."}],"url":"\/documentation\/flows\/graphprotocols\/directedgraph\/minimumcut(capacity:)"},"doc://Flows/documentation/Flows/GraphProtocols/DirectedGraph/vertexConnectivity(from:to:)":{"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"vertexConnectivity","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"from","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P6VertexQa","tex